height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Your next micro AI experiment </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/i9tY9HUvV648HxlCw1gJ6iv0Cv0=/0x0:1920x1080/1920x1080/2025/09/24/1758724642726.jpeg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of a young woman flexing a bionic robot arm\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>Your AI chatbot</strong> can do a lot more than draft emails or summarize articles. New features can turn ChatGPT, Claude and other AI tools into even better personal researchers, problem-solvers and amateur app developers.</p><ul><li><strong>Why it matters:</strong> You don't need to be a tech expert to get more out of AI. Sometimes, you just need a few practical ideas for putting it to work.</li></ul><p><strong>Inspired by</strong> The Washington Post's new guide to AI \"<a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48335954.349602/aHR0cHM6Ly93YXBvLnN0LzQ4MVFsNEI_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBe601b3a0\" target=\"_blank\">power-ups</a>,\" here are five ways to put your chatbot to work: </p><ol><li><strong>🔧 Fix something around the house:</strong> Snap a photo of a confusing error message on your dishwasher, thermostat or washing machine. Upload it with the model number, and ask AI to identify possible causes and suggest safe troubleshooting steps. I recently used AI to help authenticate a <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48335954.349602/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZHdyLmNvbS9jb2xsZWN0aW9uLXNheWwtY2hhaXI_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB54cf83db\" target=\"_blank\">Herman Miller chair</a> I bought secondhand on Facebook Marketplace, comparing its design details with changes in the chair's production over the years. </li><li><strong>🗂️ Turn a pile of documents into a personal assistant:</strong> Upload vacation itineraries, travel confirmations and reservations into a ChatGPT Project or Google's NotebookLM. Ask it to build a day-by-day schedule, flag conflicts and answer questions about your trip. My color-coded honeymoon itinerary for Argentina and Chile next month is courtesy of Claude, not my spreadsheet skills. It was <em>right </em>on the suggestion to book a rental car in Bariloche; brushing up on my Spanish is on me.</li><li><strong>🔎 Research a big purchase:</strong> Use a chatbot's Deep Research feature to compare refrigerators, mattresses or cars. Give it your budget and must-haves, and request a side-by-side breakdown of reliability, long-term costs and independent reviews. You can do the same for local services: AI helped me compare dog walkers and led me to <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48335954.349602/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucGFya3NpZGVwdXBzYmsuY29tLz91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB35ba730d\" target=\"_blank\">Parkside Pups</a>, which now walks my sweet poodle-beagle a few times a week.</li><li><strong>🛠️ Build something just for you:</strong> Want a family trivia game, holiday gift tracker or personal website? Describe it in plain English and ask AI to build a working version — no coding experience required. It's called \"vibe coding,\" and if you've checked out a journalist friend's <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48335954.349602/aHR0cHM6Ly9uYXRhbGllZGFoZXIuY29tLz91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB060f3bc7\" target=\"_blank\">portfolio lately</a>, you may have seen it in action.</li><li><strong>📑 Decode the fine print:</strong> That confusing clause buried in your 50-page homeowners insurance policy or warranty? Ask AI to explain exclusions, deductibles and coverage limits in plain English — and point you to the exact passages supporting its answers.</li></ol><p><strong>Between the lines: </strong>AI can be confidently wrong. Double-check important advice and research, and run consequential decisions by a human you trust.</p><ul><li><strong>Security is essential:</strong> Remove sensitive personal information before uploading documents, and check your chatbot's privacy settings.</li></ul><p><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48335954.349602/aHR0cHM6Ly93YXBvLnN0LzQ4MVFsNEI_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCe601b3a0\" target=\"_blank\">Gift link</a>.</em></p><ul><li><em>Have you had an experience with a chatbot lately that saved you time or taught you something? Write us at </em><a href=\"mailto:finishline@axios.com\" target=\"_blank\"><em>finishline@axios.com</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48335954.349602/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtMjYxMzk4MTYt